ining has been made available, we are concerned at the continuing absence of nationally accredited training. Its absence has meant that some staff involved in the licensing arrangements, in particular those charged with making firearms licensing decisions, have yet to receive sufficient training, commensurate with their role and responsibility","hazard":"absence of nationally accredited training for licensing decision makers"}]}],"links":[{"earlier":"https://www.judiciary.uk/prevention-of-future-death-reports/christine-lee/","later":"https://www.judiciary.uk/prevention-of-future-death-reports/maxine-davison-lee-martyn-sophie-martyn-stephen-washington-and-kate-shepherd-prevention-of-future-deaths-report/","relation":"closely_related","confidence":0.9,"explanation":"Both reports highlight a lack of adequate, nationally standardized training for police personnel responsible for firearms licensing decisions.","earlier_quote":"there was no national training course for staff working in police firearms licensing departments as Firearms Enquiry Officers","later_quote":"numerous recommendations arising from previous inquiries and reviews regarding the training of police officers and police staff involved in firearms licensing decisions had not been put into effect","promise_quote":null,"after_promise":null,"scores":{"tfidf":0.225,"embedding":0.85,"hybrid":0.6},"days_apart":1304,"same_coroner":false,"same_area":false,"later_cites_earlier":false,"earlier_has_response":false,"model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b"}],"followups":[],"dossier":null}